Ladybird now fires load at every svg element of a document, the
innermost first, right before the load event at the Window. Firefox 151
does exactly that. WebKit 26.5 fires it at the outermost svg element
only, also right before the Window’s. Chrome 158 fires it at each svg
element as it’s parsed, as SVG 1.1’s SVGLoad was, so before the Window’s
too. None of them fires it at an svg element inserted once the document
has loaded, nor does Ladybird (engine-compare).
